    "result_text": "Green. Both findings addressed.\n\n**Finding 1 (must-fix) \u2014 agreed, fixed.** Removed the dead `OwnerHousehold.of(OwnerFieldsDto)` factory and its now-unused `OwnerFieldsDto` import. The record's only caller is `AssignHousehold` via `of(Owner)`. I kept the record form itself (rather than slimming further) \u2014 it's a clean, cheap carrier and leaving it as a record keeps the \"same household\" concept named in one type; that part of the finding was explicitly optional (\"if anything\").\n\n**Finding 2 (coherence) \u2014 agreed, fixed.** `CheckPossibleDuplicate` now matches on the shared `householdId` (same household, different telephone) instead of re-deriving \"same lastName + postcode\" inline with its own, subtly different normalization. The keying rule now lives solely in `OwnerHousehold`, so a future maintainer who changes it (e.g. adds city or re-normalizes postcode) affects the possible-duplicate flag automatically. Behaviourally this is at least as correct: a non-declared same-household owner is already rejected 409 upstream by `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, and declared members return early, so the flag resolves consistently. Updated the javadoc to match.\n\nAcceptance behaviour intact \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, the acceptance test still passes.",
